  "body": "## What changed\n`setup_stock_source::a_new_block_after_a_flip_starts_from_its_own_stock_and_undoes` was red on main. The **test's expectation** was wrong; the sim code is correct. This is a test-only change.\n\n**Root cause:** neither #408 nor #410 broke anything.\n- The test also fails on #408's own branch head (d0e5d074) and on #320's first commit (1bb313d8), on macOS debug. So on this platform it never held.\n- `bits()` compares `ProgramSim.dev.dev`, the per-column `top - part`. That is a height verdict read from above.\n- After the flip, the carried body (Z 0..18) and Setup2's own block (Z −2..18) are both 60 × 60 with a top at Z18. They differ only below the part, which this verdict cannot see.\n- Face2 faced both down to Z16, the part top, so every column read exactly 0.0 in both runs.\n\n**The code path is right:**\n- `walk` takes `Entry::NewBlock` and restarts on `stock_grid(Setup2)`.\n- The test's own `incoming_body` checks already show the new block.\n- #410 doesn't touch `stock_sim` or `stock_sim_carry`.\n\n**Fix:** Setup2 now gets a distinct block (`SetStock` Box 60 × 60 × 24 at Z −2, so its top is Z22), and Face2 stops at Z19, above the part.\n- The carried run now reads `max_rest` 2 mm; the new-block run reads 3 mm. Both values are asserted.\n- The original `assert_ne!` stays, the block-volume check is now 60 × 60 × 24, and the undo/redo checks are unchanged.\n- The assertion is **stronger**: a sim that still carried after the pick would read 2 mm and fail.\n\nDecision record: `docs/decisions/415-new-block-flip.md`.\n\n## Readings\n- `setup_stock_source` 6/6, `setup_carry`, `rest_across_setups`, `stock_sim_document`, `carried_verify`, `setups` and `sim` all pass.\n- `scripts/gate.sh quick` (merged with upstream/main): app suites green.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -D warnings`: clean.\n\nChangelog: none (test-only)\n\nFixes #415\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
